{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 26.0% a year from $4.32 billion in FY2016 to $34.6 billion in FY2025 [F1][F10][F231]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The path was a step change, not a straight line: revenue rose 68.3% in FY2021 and 43.6% in FY2022, fell 3.9% in FY2023, then grew 13.7% and 34.3% in the last two years [D258][D314][D370][D426][D483]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2022 jump included the Xilinx acquisition, which brought $2.4 billion of cash and $1.6 billion of short-term investments and made Embedded revenue $4.55 billion against $246 million in FY2021 [P37][P41][S110][S109]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2025 growth was driven by Data Center and Client and Gaming, with Data Center revenue up 32% to $16.6 billion on EPYC processors and Instinct GPUs [P15][S98]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Data Center was the largest driver, contributing 15.7pp of FY2025's 34.3% growth and 48.0% of revenue [D694][D483][D692]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Client and Gaming added 19.0pp in FY2025, with Client at $10.6 billion and Gaming at $3.9 billion [D701][S124][S127]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Client revenue rose 51% on a 31% increase in processor unit shipments and a 15% increase in average selling price, and Gaming rose 51% on higher semi-custom revenue and Radeon GPU demand [P10][P9]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew 94.4% against 34.3% revenue growth, an incremental operating margin of 20.3% [D484][D483][D511]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating costs grew 10.0pp slower than revenue in FY2025, at 24.3% [D512][D504]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin of 10.7% in FY2025 sits above the 7.2% window median but far below the 22.2% FY2021 high [F60][D795][D794]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Gross margin reached a window high of 49.5%, up 0.2pp, as cost of revenue added only 0.2pp to operating margin while SG&A took 1.2pp off [F40][D800][D498][D513][D515]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The gross margin gain came from product mix, partly offset by about $440 million of net inventory and related charges tied to the MI308 export control [P14]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "In FY2025 net margin of 12.5% sat 1.9pp above the 10.7% operating margin, helped by $577 million of other income and a $103 million tax benefit [F80][F60][D843][X123][X113]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $7.71 billion was 1.78x net income in FY2025, above the 1.61x window median, and free cash flow was 1.55x net income [F110][F70][D470][D833][D471]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Operating cash flow rose on $4.3 billion of net income plus $4.6 billion of non-cash adjustments, partly offset by a $2.2 billion inventory build for Data Center products [P3]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow margin of 19.4% is near the 19.6% window high, with capex at 2.8% of revenue and 1.87x D&A [D467][D803][D466][D472]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Stock-based compensation of $1.64 billion was 21.2% of operating cash flow, down from 46.3% in FY2024 [X83][D473][D416]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Net cash reached $6.46 billion, or 18.6% of revenue, against a -17.3% peer median and in the 100th percentile of five semis peers [D476][D477][D845][D844]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Total debt rose 138% to $4.10 billion after $1.5 billion of notes were issued in March 2025, while cash and investments more than doubled to $10.6 billion [D475][P6][D474][D507]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks of $1.32 billion were 19.5% of free cash flow, and the diluted share count was flat at -0.1% [D478][D479][D506]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The current ratio of 2.85x is a window high, above the 2.19x median [F210][D812][D813]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Revenue fell 3.9% in FY2023, the only decline in the window, on a 25% drop in Client revenue and a 9% drop in Gaming [D370][P35]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "The decline was a PC inventory correction rather than a structural loss of share, and revenue has since grown 13.7% and 34.3% [P34][D426][D483]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Total debt rose 138% in FY2025 to $4.10 billion, but net cash still rose to $6.46 billion [D475][D418][D476]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "The leverage increase is modest against the cash build and does not threaten the balance sheet."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The effective tax rate moved -21.3pp to -2.5% in FY2025 on an $853 million release of uncertain tax positions [D469][D412][P4]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "The tax benefit flatters FY2025 net margin and is unlikely to repeat, so the underlying earnings base is lower than reported."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether Data Center revenue growth holds above the FY2025 32.2% rate, reported in the FY2026 10-K, would confirm the AI-driven trend [D693]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether operating margin holds above the 7.2% window median or slips toward the 1.8% FY2023 low, reported in the FY2026 10-K, would signal whether the FY2025 recovery is durable [D795][F58]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether inventory days stay below the FY2025 165 days or rise further, reported in the FY2026 10-K, would show whether the Data Center build is clearing [D481]."}
  ]}
]}
